st - simple terminal
--------------------
st is a simple terminal emulator for X and macOS which sucks less.


Requirements
------------
In order to build st you need the Xlib header files.

On macOS you need the Xcode command line tools, pkg-config and xorgproto:

    brew install pkg-config xorgproto


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (st is installed into
the /usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install st (if
necessary as root):

    make clean install

On macOS, make builds st.app into /Applications. Change APPPREFIX in
config.mk to build it somewhere else.


Running st
----------
If you did not install st with make clean install, you must compile
the st terminfo entry with the following command:

    tic -sx st.info

See the man page for additional details.

